    details = <
        ["sv"] = <
            language = <[ISO_639-1::sv]>
            purpose = <"*To record the classification system adopted by the American Society of Anesthesiologists (ASA) as part of a pre-surgical risk assessment. (en)">
            keywords = <"*ASA (en)", "*pre-operative (en)", "*surgery (en)", "*anaesthesiology (en)", "*anesthesia (en)", "*anaesthesia (en)", "*anesthesiology (en)">
            use = <"*To record the classification system adopted by the American Society of Anesthesiologists (ASA) as part of a pre-surgical risk assessment.

The ASA (2020) reference defines each classification and provides some adult, paediatric and obstetric examples to guide clinicians to assign a physical status classification level. However, because these examples are numerous and can further be refined or described at the institution level, specific examples are not included in this archetype. (en)">
            misuse = <"">
            copyright = <"© openEHR Foundation, openEHR Norway">
        >
        ["es-ar"] = <
            language = <[ISO_639-1::es-ar]>
            purpose = <"*To record the classification system adopted by the American Society of Anesthesiologists (ASA) as part of a pre-surgical risk assessment. (en)">
            keywords = <"*ASA (en)", "*pre-operative (en)", "*surgery (en)", "*anaesthesiology (en)", "*anesthesia (en)", "*anaesthesia (en)", "*anesthesiology (en)">
            use = <"*To record the classification system adopted by the American Society of Anesthesiologists (ASA) as part of a pre-surgical risk assessment.

The ASA (2020) reference defines each classification and provides some adult, paediatric and obstetric examples to guide clinicians to assign a physical status classification level. However, because these examples are numerous and can further be refined or described at the institution level, specific examples are not included in this archetype. (en)">
            misuse = <"">
            copyright = <"© openEHR Foundation, openEHR Norway">
        >
        ["nb"] = <
            language = <[ISO_639-1::nb]>
            purpose = <"For å registrere klassifikasjon vedtatt av American Society of Anesthesiologists (ASA) som del av en preoperativ risikovurdering.">
            keywords = <"ASA", "preoperativ", "kirurgi", "anestesiologi", "anestesi", "klassifisering">
            use = <"Bruk for å registrere klassifikasjonssystem vedtatt av American Society of Anesthesiologists (ASA) som del av en preoperativ risikovurdering.

Referansen til ASA (2020) definerer hver klassifikasjon og gir noen eksempler for voksne, barn og obstetriske pasienter for å veilede klinikere i å tildele et nivå av fysisk klassifikasjon. Fordi disse eksemplene er mange og kan ytterligere tilpasses eller beskrives på institusjonsnivå, er imidlertid spesifikke eksempler ikke inkludert i denne arketypen.

Norsk oversettelse av definisjoner og ASA-godkjente eksempler (se https://www.asahq.org/standards-and-practice-parameters/statement-on-asa-physical-status-classification-system). (n.d.). Retrieved December 17, 2025, from https://www.nafweb.no/assets/files/andre-dokumenter/asa-klassifisering-2025-(naf).pdf
">
            misuse = <"">
            copyright = <"© openEHR Foundation, openEHR Norway">
        >
        ["pt-br"] = <
            language = <[ISO_639-1::pt-br]>
            purpose = <"*To record the classification system adopted by the American Society of Anesthesiologists (ASA) as part of a pre-surgical risk assessment. (en)">
            keywords = <"*ASA (en)", "*pre-operative (en)", "*surgery (en)", "*anaesthesiology (en)", "*anesthesia (en)", "*anaesthesia (en)", "*anesthesiology (en)">
            use = <"*To record the classification system adopted by the American Society of Anesthesiologists (ASA) as part of a pre-surgical risk assessment.

The ASA (2020) reference defines each classification and provides some adult, paediatric and obstetric examples to guide clinicians to assign a physical status classification level. However, because these examples are numerous and can further be refined or described at the institution level, specific examples are not included in this archetype. (en)">
            misuse = <"">
            copyright = <"© openEHR Foundation, openEHR Norway">
        >
        ["en"] = <
            language = <[ISO_639-1::en]>
            purpose = <"To record the classification system adopted by the American Society of Anesthesiologists (ASA) as part of a pre-surgical risk assessment.">
            keywords = <"ASA", "pre-operative", "surgery", "anaesthesiology", "anesthesia", "anaesthesia", "anesthesiology">
            use = <"To record the classification system adopted by the American Society of Anesthesiologists (ASA) as part of a pre-surgical risk assessment.

The ASA (2020) reference defines each classification and provides some adult, paediatric and obstetric examples to guide clinicians to assign a physical status classification level. However, because these examples are numerous and can further be refined or described at the institution level, specific examples are not included in this archetype.">
            misuse = <"">
            copyright = <"© openEHR Foundation, openEHR Norway">
        >
        ["es"] = <
            language = <[ISO_639-1::es]>
            purpose = <"Registrar el sistema de clasificación adoptado por la Sociedad Americana de Anestesiólogos (ASA) como parte de la evaluación de riesgos prequirúrgicos.">
            keywords = <"ASA(en): Sociedad Americana de Anestesiólogos.", "pre-operative(en): preoperatorio.", "surgery(en): cirugía.", "anaesthesiology(en): anestesiología.", "anesthesia(en): anestesia.", "anaesthesia(en): anestesia.", "anesthesiology(en): anestesiología.">
            use = <"La referencia de la ASA (2020) define cada clasificación y proporciona algunos ejemplos en adultos, pediatría y obstetricia para guiar a los clínicos en la asignación de un nivel de clasificación de estado físico. Sin embargo, dado que estos ejemplos son numerosos y pueden ser redefinidos o descritos a nivel institucional, ejemplos específicos no se incluyen en este arquetipo.">
            misuse = <"">
            copyright = <"© openEHR Foundation, openEHR Norway">
        >
        ["nl"] = <
            language = <[ISO_639-1::nl]>
            purpose = <"Voor het vastleggen van het classificatiesysteem van de American Society of Anesthesiologists (ASA) als onderdeel van een preoperatieve risicobeoordeling.">
            keywords = <"ASA", "preoperatief", "chirurgie", "anesthesiologie", "anesthesie">
            use = <"Voor het vastleggen van het classificatiesysteem van de American Society of Anesthesiologists (ASA) als onderdeel van een preoperatieve risicobeoordeling.

De ASA (2020)-referentie definieert elke classificatie en geeft enkele voorbeelden voor volwassenen, kinderen en obstetrie om zorgverleners te helpen een classificatieniveau voor de fysieke status toe te kennen. Omdat deze voorbeelden talrijk zijn en op instellingsniveau verder verfijnd of beschreven kunnen worden, zijn specifieke voorbeelden niet in dit archetype opgenomen.">
            misuse = <"">
        >
    >

definition
    OBSERVATION[at0000] matches {    -- ASA physical status classification system
        data matches {
            HISTORY[at0015] matches {
                events cardinality matches {1..*; unordered} matches {
                    POINT_EVENT[at0016] matches {    -- Any point in time event
                        data matches {
                            ITEM_TREE[at0017] matches {
                                items cardinality matches {1..*; unordered} matches {
                                    ELEMENT[at0001] occurrences matches {0..1} matches {    -- Classification
                                        value matches {
                                            DV_ORDINAL[at9003] matches {
                                                [value, symbol] matches {
                                                    [{1}, {[at0003]}],    -- ASA 1
                                                    [{2}, {[at0004]}],    -- ASA 2
                                                    [{3}, {[at0005]}],    -- ASA 3
                                                    [{4}, {[at0006]}],    -- ASA 4
                                                    [{5}, {[at0007]}],    -- ASA 5
                                                    [{6}, {[at0008]}]    -- ASA 6
                                                }
                                            }
                                        }
                                    }
                                    ELEMENT[at0020] occurrences matches {0..1} matches {    -- Emergency (E)
                                        value matches {
                                            DV_BOOLEAN[at9004] matches {
                                                value matches {True}
                                            }
                                        }
                                    }
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
        protocol matches {
            ITEM_TREE[at0018] matches {
                items cardinality matches {0..*; unordered} matches {
                    allow_archetype CLUSTER[at0019]    -- Extension
                }
            }
        }
    }

terminology
    term_definitions = <
        ["sv"] = <
            ["at0000"] = <
                text = <"*ASA physical status classification system(en)">
                description = <"*Classification system adopted by the American Society of Anesthesiologists (ASA) as part of a pre-surgical risk assessment. (en)">
            >
            ["at0001"] = <
                text = <"*Classification(en)">
                description = <"*Assessed classification of a patient.(en)">
                comment = <"*Examples for each class can be found in the ASA (2020) reference. (en)">
            >
            ["at0016"] = <
                text = <"Tidsobestämd händelse">
                description = <"Händelse vid ospecificerad tidpunkt, där tiden kan anges explicit i en template, eller genereras automatiskt av vissa IT-system.">
            >
            ["at0019"] = <
                text = <"Tilläggsinformation">
                description = <"Plats för att infoga tilläggsinformation som krävs för lokala anpassningar eller anpassning till andra referensmodeller eller formella krav.">
                comment = <"Exempelvis lokala informationskrav eller metadata för anpassning till FHIR-motsvarigheter.">
            >
            ["at0020"] = <
                text = <"*Emergency (E)(en)">
                description = <"*Record as True if the surgery was carried out in an emergency situation. (en)">
                comment = <"*Represented by the suffix 'E' added to the class. For example: '3E'. Class 5 is usually an emergency and is therefore almost always only designated as '5E'. The class '6E' is not valid and is simply recorded as class '6', as all organ retrieval in brain-dead patients is done urgently. Definition of an emergency can be found in the ASA (2020) reference. (en)">
            >
            ["at0003"] = <
                text = <"*ASA I (en)">
                description = <"*A normal healthy patient. (en)">
            >
            ["at0004"] = <
                text = <"*ASA II (en)">
                description = <"*A patient with mild systemic disease. (en)">
            >
            ["at0005"] = <
                text = <"*ASA III (en)">
                description = <"*A patient with severe systemic disease. (en)">
            >
            ["at0006"] = <
                text = <"*ASA IV (en)">
                description = <"*A patient with severe systemic disease that is a constant threat to life. (en)">
            >
            ["at0007"] = <
                text = <"*ASA V (en)">
                description = <"*A moribund patient who is not expected to survive without the operation. (en)">
            >
            ["at0008"] = <
                text = <"*ASA VI (en)">
                description = <"*A declared brain-dead patient whose organs are being removed for donor purposes. (en)">
            >
            ["ac9001"] = <
                text = <"*Classification(en) (synthesised)">
                description = <"*Assessed classification of a patient.(en) (synthesised)">
            >
        >
        ["nb"] = <
            ["at0000"] = <
                text = <"ASA-klassifikasjon">
                description = <"Klassifikasjonssystem vedtatt av American Society of Anesthesiologists (ASA) som del av en preoperativ risikovurdering.">
            >
            ["at0001"] = <
                text = <"Klassifikasjon">
                description = <"Vurdert klassifikasjon av en pasient.">
                comment = <"Eksempler for hver klasse kan ses i referansen til ASA (2020).">
            >
            ["at0003"] = <
                text = <"ASA I">
                description = <"En normal frisk pasient.">
            >
            ["at0004"] = <
                text = <"ASA II">
                description = <"En pasient med mild systemsykdom.">
            >
            ["at0005"] = <
                text = <"ASA III">
                description = <"En pasient med alvorlig systemsykdom.">
            >
            ["at0006"] = <
                text = <"ASA IV">
                description = <"En pasient med alvorlig systemsykdom som er kontinuerlig livstruende.">
            >
            ["at0007"] = <
                text = <"ASA V">
                description = <"En døende pasient som ikke forventes å overleve uten operasjonen.">
            >
            ["at0008"] = <
                text = <"ASA VI">
                description = <"En erklært hjernedød pasient til uttak av organer for donasjon.">
            >
            ["at0016"] = <
                text = <"Uspesifisert tidspunkthendelse">
                description = <"Uspesifisert tidspunkt som kan defineres mer eksplisitt i en templat eller i en applikasjon.">
            >
            ["at0019"] = <
                text = <"Tilleggsinformasjon">
                description = <"Ytterligere informasjon som trengs for å kunne registrere lokalt definert innhold eller for å tilpasse til andre referansemodeller eller formalismer.">
                comment = <"For eksempel lokale informasjonsbehov eller ytterligere metadata for å kunne tilpasse til tilsvarende konsepter i FHIR.">
            >
            ["at0020"] = <
                text = <"Ø-hjelp">
                description = <"Registrer som True dersom operasjonen ble utført i en akuttsituasjon.">
                comment = <"Representert ved suffikset \"E\" som legges til klassifiseringen. For eksempel: \"3E\". Klassifiseringen 5 er vanligvis en akuttsituasjon og betegnes derfor nesten alltid kun som \"5E\". Klassifiseringen 6E er ikke gyldig og registreres bare som klassifisering \"6\", ettersom all organuthenting fra hjernedøde pasienter skjer akutt. Definisjonen av en akuttsituasjon finnes i ASA-referansen (2020).">
            >
            ["ac9001"] = <
                text = <"Klassifikasjon (synthesised)">
                description = <"Vurdert klassifikasjon av en pasient. (synthesised)">
            >
        >
        ["es-ar"] = <
            ["at0000"] = <
                text = <"*ASA physical status classification system (en)">
                description = <"*Classification system adopted by the American Society of Anesthesiologists (ASA) as part of a pre-surgical risk assessment. (en)">
            >
            ["at0001"] = <
                text = <"*Classification (en)">
                description = <"*Assessed classification of a patient. (en)">
                comment = <"*Examples for each class can be found in the ASA (2020) reference. (en)">
            >
            ["at0016"] = <
                text = <"Point in time">
                description = <"Fecha y/o hora que puede ser explícitamente definida en una plantilla o en tiempo de ejecución.">
            >
            ["at0019"] = <
                text = <"Extensión">
                description = <"Información adicional requerida para contemplar contenidos locales o para alinear con otros modelos o formalismos de referencia">
                comment = <"ejemplo: requerimientos locales de información o metadatos adicionales necesarios para el alineamiento con FHIR.">
            >
            ["at0020"] = <
                text = <"*Emergency (E) (en)">
                description = <"*Record as True if the surgery was carried out in an emergency situation. (en)">
                comment = <"*Represented by the suffix 'E' added to the class. For example: '3E'. Class 5 is usually an emergency and is therefore almost always only designated as '5E'. The class '6E' is not valid and is simply recorded as class '6', as all organ retrieval in brain-dead patients is done urgently. Definition of an emergency can be found in the ASA (2020) reference. (en)">
            >
            ["at0003"] = <
                text = <"*ASA I (en)">
                description = <"*A normal healthy patient. (en)">
            >
            ["at0004"] = <
                text = <"*ASA II (en)">
                description = <"*A patient with mild systemic disease. (en)">
            >
            ["at0005"] = <
                text = <"*ASA III (en)">
                description = <"*A patient with severe systemic disease. (en)">
